From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 03:38:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] web-app: sticker suggestions for a typed emoji (experimental)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Settings → Experimental → Composer → "Sticker suggestions" (off by
default, experimentalStickerSuggestions). When the draft is exactly one
emoji (one grapheme, U+FE0F ignored) with no attachment and not in edit
mode, a strip above the input lists the stickers associated with that
emoji (core sticker packs: emojis per sticker). Tapping one sends it the
same way the picker does and then clears the input, but only if the text
at that moment still is exactly that emoji; otherwise nothing is sent or
cleared and the strip goes away. Enter still sends the text; Escape hides
the strip until the text changes; pressing a suggestion keeps the
input's focus.

useDraft: removeQuote and updateDraftText built the new draft from a stale
snapshot, so two edits in one event (send with a quote, then clear) brought
the quote back; both now build on the latest draft via a ref.
